      "task_outcome_short": "Screened 100 studies from the chunk. 53 studies were INCLUDED and 47 studies were          
  EXCLUDED based on the selection criteria for prospective trials and observational cohort studies evaluating           
  metformin in type 2 diabetes patients compared to placebo or other glucose-lowering therapies.",                      
      "task_outcome_detailed": "Completed title/abstract screening for 100 studies (indices 1-100) from the systematic  
  review on 'Risk of fatal and nonfatal lactic acidosis with metformin use in type 2 diabetes mellitus'. Selection      
  criteria required: (1) Prospective trials or observational cohort studies, (2) Patients with type 2 diabetes of at    
  least one month duration, (3) Evaluation of metformin alone or in combination, (4) Comparison to placebo or other     
  glucose-lowering therapy.\n\nINCLUDED (53 studies): Studies meeting all criteria including RCTs comparing metformin   
  vs placebo, metformin vs other glucose-lowering agents (sulfonylureas, thiazolidinediones, insulin, etc.),            
  combination therapies with metformin, and prospective observational cohorts with comparison groups. Key included      
  studies: #3, #4, #5, #7, #8, #9, #14, #15, #17, #19, #20, #21, #22, #25, #26, #27, #28, #29, #32, #33, #34, #35,      
  #36, #38, #39, #40, #42, #44, #45, #46, #47, #50, #52, #56, #61, #65, #66, #68, #70, #74, #75, #77, #78, #82, #87,    
  #88, #91, #92, #94, #95, #97, #98, #100.\n\nEXCLUDED (47 studies): Studies excluded for various reasons: (1)          
  Single-arm before/after designs without control groups (#2, #24, #54, #55, #60, #62, #63, #64, #67, #85), (2)         
  Metformin as constant background therapy while evaluating other interventions (#1, #11, #16, #23, #31, #37, #51,      
  #57, #69, #72, #80, #83, #99), (3) Case reports/series/reviews (#10, #13, #41, #76, #79, #84, #86, #90), (4) Wrong    
  study population (type 1 diabetes) (#81, #89), (5) Retrospective designs (#48), (6) Abstract/content mismatches       
  (#18, #59), (7) Comparing only biguanides to each other (#30, #96), (8) Comparing metformin to non-glucose-lowering   
  agents (#93).\n\nConfidence levels: Most decisions were made with HIGH confidence. MEDIUM confidence assigned to      
  studies where design details were less clear from abstract alone (#52, #56, #78, #95).",                              
      "additional_context": "The screening followed conservative principles - when in doubt, studies were included.     
  The review objective focuses on lactic acidosis incidence and blood lactate levels, but the selection criteria are    
